{
  "dom_id": "step-q347187",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=\u27e87{t}^{2},\\,-18\u27e9,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=5.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$v(5)=\u27e8${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-18)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e814t,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=5,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(5) & =\u27e814(5),\\,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e870,\\,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
